    "chunk_text": "33A. (1) Where an employer who isdissatisfied with an order of a Magistrate\u2019sCourt on any written complaint made by theCommissioner-General under section 136B ofthe Code of Criminal Procedure Act, No. 15 of1979 against such employer, due to any failureto comply with an order of a tribunal, an awardof an industrial court or an arbitrator which hasbeen made in favor of a workman, makes anapplication to invoke the revisionaryjurisdiction of the High Court establisded underArticle 154P of the Constitution, in respect ofsuch order, shall at the time of such applicationfurnish to the relevant Magistrate\u2019s Court, asecurity of an amount equal to such sum in cash,where the order which is the subject of suchapplication directs the payment of a sum ofmoney to the worker.\n\n(3) Every application made under subsection(1) shall be supported by a certificate under thehand of the Registrar of the relevantMagistrate\u2019s Court to the effect that the securityas specified in subsection (1) has been dulyfurnished by such employer.\n\n\u201cEmployer tofurnish asecurity inrespect of anapplication tothe High Court\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n30\n\nInsertion ofsection 33A inthe principalenactment\n\nIndustrial Disputes (Amendment)4\n\n(4) The Commissioner-General shall refundthe sum furnished under subsection (1) togetherwith the interest on that sum to the relevantparty in accordance with the final order of theHigh Court established under Article 154p, theCourt of Appeal or the Supreme Court, as thecase may be.\u201d.\n\n5. In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nSinhala text toprevail in caseofinconsistency\n\n5\n\nIndustrial Disputes (Amendment)5\n\nDepartment of Government Printing"
