    "chunk_text": "Clause 9 : This clause amends section 66 of the principal enactment and the legal effectof this section as amended is to remove the definition of the expression \u201cminor\u201d consequentto the amendment made by clause 2.\n\nKandyan Marriage and Divorce(Amendment)1\n\n5\n\nL.D.\u2013O. 73/2021\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Kandyan Marriage andDivorce (Amendment) Act, No. of 2022.\n\n2.Part II (sections 8, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13, 14 and 15) of theKandyan Marriage and Divorce Act (Chapter 113)(hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) is herebyrepealed.\n\n3.Section 16 of the principal enactment is herebyamended as follows:-\n\n(1) by the repeal of sub-paragraph (b) of paragraph (6)thereof; and\n\n(2) in paragraph (7) thereof\u2013\n\n(a) by the substitution, in sub-paragraph (a)thereof, for the word \u201ccorrect;\u201d, of the words\u201ccorrect; and\u201d;\n\n(b) by the substitution, in sub-parapraph (b)thereof, for the word \u201cmarriage;\u201d, of the word\u201cmarriage.\u201d; and\n\n(c) by the repeal of sub-parapraphs (c) and (d)thereof.\n\n4.Section 18 of the principal enactment is herebyamended, by the repeal of paragraph (5) thereof and thesubstitution therefor, of the following paragraph:-\n\n\u201c(5) (a) Any party to the marriage who desires to obtain amarriage notice certificate from a District Registrar\n\nShort title\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\nAmendmentof section 16of theprincipalenactment\n\nRepeal ofPart II ofChapter 113\n\nAmendmentof section 18of theprincipalenactment\n\n2Kandyan Marriage and Divorce(Amendment)\n\nbefore the expiry of the period referred to inparagraph (3) (a) (i) or paragraph (4) (a) (i) orparagraph (4) (c) (ii) of this section shall appear inperson before that Registrar and make and subscribea declaration to the effect that there is no lawfulimpediment or other lawful hindrance to themarriage."
