    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by Hon. Eran Wickramaratne, M.P. on 09th of June, 2023\n\n(Published in the Gazette on May 29, 2023)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n2-2dp\n\n2-\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 10.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\n[Bill No. 182]\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nBILL\n\nA\n\nVALUE ADDED TAX (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Value Added Tax Act, No. 14 of 2002\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nThis Bill amends section 2A of the Principal Enactment so as to ensure that any Ordermade by the Minister thereunder will come into force only upon the approval thereof byParliament.\n\nValue Added Tax (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE VALUE ADDED TAX ACT, NO. 14 OF 2002\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows:-\n\n1.This Act may be cited as the Value Added Tax(Amendment) Act, No. of 2023.\n\n2.Section 2A of the Value Added Tax Act, No.14 of2002 (hereinafter referred to as the \u201cprincipal enactment\u201d) ishereby amended by the deletion of subsections (2), (3), (4)and (5) thereof, and the substitution therefor of the followingnew subsections which shall take effect as subsections (2)and (3) thereof:-\n\n\u201c(2)Every such Order shall be published in the Gazette,and shall as soon as convenient thereafter be placedbefore Parliament for its approval.\n\n(3)Such Order shall only come into force upon itsapproval by Parliament.\u201d.\n\n3.In the event of any inconsistency between the Sinhalaand Tamil texts of this Act, the Sinhala text shall prevail.\n\nShort title\n\nAmendmentof section 2Aof Act No.14of 2002\n\nSinhala textto prevail incase ofinconsistency\n\n2Value Added Tax (Amendment)\n\nDEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING"
