    "chunk_text": "(h) Inspection of accounts;\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n8Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n(5)Metting of the Board of Management:\u2013\n\n(a) The appointments of the Board ofManagement shall be in force for a period oftwo years;\n\n(c) If it has been delayed to appoint such a newBoard, it shall be a fixed rule not to carry outany projects, or perform or carry out any otheractivities;\n\n(d) It shall be necessary to hold a general meetingat least once in every three months and noresolution and decision shall be made unlessthere is the majority power of more than onethird including the absentees to the generalmeeting;\n\n(e) The registrar may not fail to convene a generalmeeting in response to a written request madeby one third of the members;\n\n(f) Every Board of Management shall submit adevelopment plan for the subsequent two yearswitin a period of month upon their newappointment.\n\n6. (1) The Foundation shall have its own fund and shallbe utilized for the activities and for the provision of theproposed projects thereof.\n\nOrganizationalFund\n\n25\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n9Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n(2)All moneys recieved by war of gift, bequest ,donation, subscription, contribution, fees or grants for andon account of the Foundation shall be deposited in one ormore public banks, as determined by the Board ofManagement to the credit of the Foundation.\n\n(3) There shall be established a depreciation fund and asinking fund for the rehabilitation, development andimprovement of the property.\n\n(4)There shall be paid out of the Fund, all sum of moneyas are required to defray any expenditure incurred by theFoundation in the exercise, performance and discharge ofits powers, duties and functions under the Act.\n\n7. (1) The Foundation shall cause proper accounts to bekept of its income and expenditure.\n\n(2) The account or accounts shall be audited annually bythe auditor of the Foundation.\n\n(3)The financial year of the Foundation shall beconsidered from the First (1st) of January to Thirty First(31st) of December every year."
