    "chunk_size_bytes": 2080,
    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPrice : Rs. 30.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nBILL\n\nA\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs and ConstitutionalReforms on 18th of July, 2023\n\n(Published in the Gazette on June 27, 2023)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014[Bill No. 188]\n\nCONTEMPT OF A COURT, TRIBUNAL OR INSTITUTION\n\nto provide for the uniform application of the law relating to the contempt ofa court, tribunal or institution; to provide for the procedure in punishingthe contempt of a court, tribunal or institution; and to provide for mattersconnected therewith or incidental thereto\n\n1Contempt of a Court,Tribunal or Institution\n\n5\n\n10\n\nL.D.- O. 55/2021\n\nAN ACT TO PROVIDE FOR THE UNIFORM APPLICATION OF THE LAW RELATING\n\nTO THE CONTEMPT OF A COURT, TRIBUNAL OR INSTITUTION; TO PROVIDE\n\nFOR THE PROCEDURE IN PUNISHING THE CONTEMPT OF A COURT,\n\nTRIBUNAL OR INSTITUTION; AND TO PROVIDE FOR MATTERS CONNECTED\n\nTHEREWITH OR INCIDENTAL THERETO.\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows: -\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Contempt of a Court,Tribunal or Institution Act, No. of 2023.\n\n2. The objects of this Act shall be to:-\n\n(a) uphold the dignity and authority of a court,tribunal and institution;\n\n(b) protect the due administration of justice;\n\n(c) ensure adherence to judicial directives;\n\n(d) preserve and maintain the effectiveness andimpartiality of a court, tribunal and institution;\n\n(e) safeguard public order, public health and morals;\n\n(f) strike a balance between the right of expression,fair comment and compliance with judicialdirectives;\n\n(g) set out with precision the ambit of contempt of acourt, tribunal and institution; and\n\n(h) ensure the observance of, and respect for, thedue process of law.\n\n15\n\nShort title"
