    "chunk_text": "PARLIAMENT OF THE DEMOCRATICSOCIALIST REPUBLIC OFSRI LANKA\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\n[Bill No. 194]\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nPresented by the Minister of Justice, Prison Affairs andConstitutional Reforms on 08th of August, 2023\n\n(Published in the Gazette on July 19, 2023)\n\nOrdered by Parliament to be printed\n\nA\n\nBILL\n\nPRINTED AT THE DEPARTMENT OF GOVERNMENT PRINTING, SRI LANKA\n\nTO BE PURCHASED AT THE GOVERNMENT PUBLICATIONS BUREAU, COLOMBO 5\n\nPrice : Rs. 12.00Postage : Rs. 150.00\n\n\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\u2014\n\nThis Bill can be downloaded from www.documents.gov.lk\n\nCIVIL PROCEDURE CODE (AMENDMENT)\n\nto amend the Civil Procedure Code ( Chapter 101)\n\nSTATEMENT OF LEGAL EFFECT\n\nClause 2 : This clause amends section 205 of the Civil Procedure Code (Chapter 101)and the legal effect of this section as amended is to provide for-\n\n(a)the issuance of one certified copy of the judgement or final decree of an actionto each party free of charge, where the respective parties to such action applyfor the same; and\n\n(b)the recongnition of a document issued or transmitted by a court electronically,as signed and sealed documents and the electronic signature of the Registrar,court and other authorized officers.\n\nCivil Procedure Code (Amendment)1\n\n5\n\n10\n\nL.D.\u2013O. 44/2017\n\nAN ACT TO AMEND THE CIVIL PROCEDURE CODE (CHAPTER 101)\n\nBE it enacted by the Parliament of the Democratic SocialistRepublic of Sri Lanka as follows :-\n\n1. This Act may be cited as the Civil Procedure Code(Amendment) Act, No. of 2023.\n\n2. The Civil Procedure Code (Chapter 101) is herebyamended by the repeal of section 205 thereof and substitutiontherefor of the following section:-\n\n205. (1) The Registrar of the court shall,where the respective parties to an action applyfor a certified copy of the judgement or finaldecree of the action, issue one certified copyof the same to each such party free of charge.\n\n(2) Subject to the provisions of subsection(1), the Registrar of the court shall, upon anyperson-"
