    "chunk_size_bytes": 2024,
    "chunk_text": "(i)pioneering and evaluating human thoughts andfeelings of all types of arts and crafts, aesthetics,their apreciation and undrstanding and identifyingand disposing obstacles existing against theirdissemination;\n\n3Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(k)engaging in activities which are not specifiedabove, which are incidentally accepted and anyother matters which are understood without delay.\n\n4.Subject to the provisions of this Act and any otherwritten law, the Foundation shall have the power\u2013\n\n(a) to request and receive contributions, grants,donations and gifts of all forms as may be necessaryfor the purpose of the Foundation;\n\n(b) to purchase, rent, lease or otherwise obtain lands orbuildings which may be required for the purpose ofthe Foundation;\n\n(c) to borrow or raise funds with or without interest forthe purposes of the Foundation;\n\n(d) to make, draw, accept, discount, endorse, buy, selland issue bills of exchange, cheques, promissorynotes and other negotiable instruments and to open,operate, maintain and close accounts in any bank;\n\n(e) to invest any funds that are not immediately requiredfor the purposes of the Foundation, in such manneras the Executive Council may deem necessary;\n\n(f) to enter into agreement or contracts with any personor any company or body of persons with a view topromoting the objects of the Foundation;\n\nPowers of theFoundation\n\n4Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n25\n\n(g) to undertake, accept, execute, perform andadminister any lawful trust or any condition thatmay affect any movable or immovable property;\n\n(h) to appoint, employ, dismiss or terminate the servicesof officers and servants of the Foundation and topay them such salaries, allowances and gratuities asmay be determined by the Foundation; and\n\n(i) to do all other things as are necessary or expedientfor the proper and effective carrying out of theobjects of the Foundation;\n\n(j) It is the responsibility of every member to obey therecongnized rules of the Foundation."
