    "chunk_text": "(h) Inspection of accounts;\n\n5\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n8Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n5\n\n(5)Meetings of the Board of Management\u2013\n\n(a) The appointments of the Board ofManagement shall be in force for a period oftwo years;\n\n(c) If it has been delayed to appoint such a newBoard, it shall be a fixed rule not to carry outany projects, or perform or carry out any otheractivities;\n\n(d) It shall be necessary to hold a general meetingat least once in every three months and noresolution and decision shall be made unlessthere is the majority power of more than onethird including the absentees to the generalmeeting;\n\n(e) The registrar may not fail to convene a generalmeeting in response to a written request madeby one third of the members;\n\n(f) Every Board of Management shall submit adevelopment plan for the subsequent two yearswithin a period of month upon their newappointment.\n\n6. (1) The Foundation shall have its own fund and shallbe utilized for the activities and for the provision of theproposed projects thereof.\n\nOrganizationalFund\n\n25\n\n10\n\n15\n\n20\n\n9Janaraja Foundation (Incorporation)\n\n(2) All moneys received by way of gifts, bequests , donations,subscriptions, contributions, fees or grants for and on account of theFoundation shall be deposited in one or more public banks, asdetermined by the Board of Management to the credit of theFoundation.\n\n(3) There shall be established a depreciation fund and a sinkingfund for the rehabilitation, development and improvement of theproperty.\n\n(4) There shall be paid out of the Fund, all sums of money as arerequired to defray any expenditure incurred by the Foundation in theexercise, performance and discharge of its powers, duties andfunctions under the Act.\n\n7. (1) The Foundation shall cause proper accounts to be kept ofits income and expenditure.\n\n(2) The account or accounts shall be audited annually by theauditor of the Foundation.\n\n(3)The financial year of the Foundation shall be consideredfrom the First (1st) of January to Thirty First (31st) of Decemberevery year."
